{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":51.4900016784668,"text":"Parnassus is not one-pointed peak, but a whole massif, and its highest point is called Liakoura, at 2,457 meters. In the myths, it was the Mountain of the Muses and of Apollo, and when the Great Flood covered the world, Deucalion's Ark came to rest here. In reality, it is a limestone mountain, full of caves and sinkholes, and rainwater does not run down its surface, it goes inside it, travels in the dark, and comes out lower down as springs. Castalia is one of them, which means the water the Pythia drank before speaking had first traveled through the whole mountain. In winter, the summit is covered with snow that lasts into spring, and from the top, you can see the Gulf of Corinth to the south, and central Greece spreading away to the north at the same time.","words":[{"word":"Parnassus","start":0,"end":0.9200000166893005},{"word":"is","start":0.9200000166893005,"end":1.2200000286102295},{"word":"not","start":1.2200000286102295,"end":1.559999942779541},{"word":"one","start":1.559999942779541,"end":1.9600000381469727},{"word":"pointed","start":1.9600000381469727,"end":2.619999885559082},{"word":"peak","start":2.619999885559082,"end":2.6600000858306885},{"word":"but","start":2.9800000190734863,"end":3.180000066757202},{"word":"a","start":3.180000066757202,"end":3.3399999141693115},{"word":"whole","start":3.3399999141693115,"end":3.640000104904175},{"word":"massif","start":3.640000104904175,"end":4.179999828338623},{"word":"and","start":4.639999866485596,"end":4.760000228881836},{"word":"its","start":4.760000228881836,"end":4.920000076293945},{"word":"highest","start":4.920000076293945,"end":5.300000190734863},{"word":"point","start":5.300000190734863,"end":5.599999904632568},{"word":"is","start":5.599999904632568,"end":5.840000152587891},{"word":"called","start":5.840000152587891,"end":6.159999847412109},{"word":"Liakoura","start":6.159999847412109,"end":6.699999809265137},{"word":"at","star